HST Office: the ribbon (Tabbed notebookbar) in the frame coat of the HST look, and a paint-only button look
for other toolboxes (the sidebar's tab bar).

- One switch: the ribbon takes the frame coat while HSTRibbon/OwnerDraw and HSTAppearance FrameCoat/Ribbon
  are on (and the coat itself, UiCoat/Enabled or HST_UI_COAT) and high contrast is off
  (hst::ribbon::coatActive). Otherwise it draws exactly as before.
- Surface: the tab control of the notebookbar is one flat aFrameSurface (no gradient, D13) on every
  platform, the native tab pane/header no longer drawn, with one whole-pixel aFrameDivider row along its
  bottom edge, between the ribbon and the document.
- Pages (hst::ribbon::CoatPages, from the notebookbar tab control at its first show, after its layout and
  after a theme or high-contrast change): a page's background is aFrameSurface (its control background, so
  its native/coat tab body and every transparent child show the surface); its groups' vertical separators
  draw a plain line of one device pixel in aFrameDivider and its captions are in aMuted, or in the ribbon's
  caption colour where aMuted does not reach 4.5:1 on the surface (light: 4.46:1). FixedLine and FixedText
  ask hst::ribbon::CoatColor when they paint, so the colours follow the theme and high contrast at once; a
  caption with a colour of its own keeps it. Caption font size unchanged (no layout change).
- Buttons: hover aHover, pressed aPressed, checked aPill with a 1 px aSelectedIndicator border, radius
  Control, through hst::design::DrawRoundRect (crisp on Skia/GDI/Cairo/Quartz); a large split button's two
  parts divided by aFrameDivider. Their items' erase no longer fills a highlighted item with a theme
  colour first (the rounded shape lies on the surface).
- Tabs (D6): the selected tab's underline size::TabIndicator thick in aSelectedIndicator under its label, a
  light aHover pill under the mouse; tab labels in aText; contextual tabs keep their accent band and colour,
  the File button its brand colours.
- hst::ribbon::SetButtonLook(ToolBox& or weld::Toolbar&, ButtonLook::SidebarTab): read only in ToolBox::ImplDrawButton, no
  size change. While FrameCoat/Sidebar is active the open deck's tab is an aPill pill with a TabIndicator
  wide aSelectedIndicator bar on its leading edge (as the gtk3 sidebar CSS), hover aHover, pressed aPressed.
- The ribbon's GTK CSS fragment stays empty (the ribbon is VCL on gtk3 too).
- No size, order, collapse ladder, keytip, tooltip, banner or accessible-name change.
- CppunitTest_vcl_hst_ribbon_coat: button, tab, surface and divider pixels in the tokens, light and dark;
  contrast of captions and dividers; a page's surface and captions and their rollback; the switches and
  high contrast; the sidebar tab look and the toolbox size it keeps.

